---

<div class="project-details">
  <h2>ManageSmartr — Operations & Order Management Platform</h2>

  <p>
    ManageSmartr is a comprehensive web platform built to modernize and
    streamline the workflow of steel wall delivery operations. The system
    centralizes order management, client collaboration, and internal operations
    into a single, role-based application used daily by administrators, clients,
    and field employees.
  </p>

  <p class="mt-2 text-sm">
    Company: Built Smartr<br />
    Role: Tech Lead / Senior Frontend Engineer<br />
    Team: 1 Tech Lead (me), 2 Junior Developers, 1 Intermediate Developer<br />
    Period: October 2025 - December 2025
  </p>

  <div class="w-full bg-gray-400 h-[1px] my-5 md:my-10"></div>

  <h3>My Role & Leadership</h3>

  <p>
    As the Tech Lead, I was responsible for both the technical direction and the
    day-to-day execution of the project. I assumed ownership of the most complex
    architectural decisions, critical features, and performance-sensitive flows,
    while also leading and mentoring the development team.
  </p>

  <ul>
    <li>
      Defined the overall frontend architecture using <strong
        >Next.js App Router</strong
      >
      and established scalable patterns for routing, layouts, and role-based access.
    </li>
    <li>
      Implemented the most complex application areas, including authentication
      flows, role-based dashboards, and real-time order state handling.
    </li>
    <li>
      Led code reviews, guided juniors on best practices, and ensured consistent
      code quality across the team.
    </li>
    <li>
      Translated business requirements into clear technical tasks and
      milestones, balancing delivery speed with long-term maintainability.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <div class="w-full bg-gray-400 h-[1px] my-5 md:my-10"></div>

  <h3>Technical Overview</h3>

  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Frontend & Platform:</strong> Built with
      <strong>Next.js 15</strong> (App Router) and <strong>TypeScript</strong>,
      focusing on scalability, performance, and a clean separation of concerns
      between admin, client, and employee portals.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Role-Based Interfaces:</strong> Designed and implemented distinct experiences
      for <strong>Admins</strong>, <strong>Clients</strong>,
      <strong>Sales</strong>, <strong>Manufacturers</strong>, and
      <strong>Drivers</strong>, each with tailored permissions and workflows.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>State & Data Management:</strong> Used
      <strong>Zustand</strong> for predictable client-side state and
      <strong>Supabase</strong> for authentication, database access, and real-time
      data.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>UI & Design System:</strong> Established a consistent design system
      using <strong>Tailwind CSS</strong>, <strong>Radix UI</strong>, and
      <strong>Shadcn UI</strong>, ensuring accessibility and reusability.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Forms & Validation:</strong> Implemented robust form handling with
      <strong>React Hook Form</strong> and <strong>Zod</strong>, reducing errors
      and improving data integrity across complex workflows.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <div class="w-full bg-gray-400 h-[1px] my-5 md:my-10"></div>

  <h3>Key Features Delivered</h3>

  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Admin Dashboard:</strong> Centralized control over clients, projects,
      orders, PDFs, and system-wide metrics.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Client Portal:</strong> Kanban-based order tracking, order creation,
      modification requests, and real-time status visibility.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Employee Views:</strong> Purpose-built screens for sales, manufacturing,
      and delivery drivers, optimized for clarity and speed.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>End-to-End Order Lifecycle:</strong> From order creation to delivery,
      with clear status transitions and role-aware actions.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <div class="w-full bg-gray-400 h-[1px] my-5 md:my-10"></div>

  <p class="mb-4">
    <strong>Key Skills:</strong> Next.js, TypeScript, Supabase, Tailwind CSS, Zustand,
    React Hook Form, Zod, System Architecture, Technical Leadership.
  </p>

  <p class="mb-3">
    <strong>Impact:</strong> ManageSmartr significantly improved operational clarity
    and reduced friction between clients, administrators, and field employees. By
    introducing clear role separation, real-time visibility, and a scalable frontend
    architecture, the platform enabled smoother collaboration and faster decision-making
    across the entire delivery pipeline.
  </p>

  <p>
    This project highlights my ability to lead a team, take ownership of complex
    technical challenges, and deliver a production-ready platform that balances
    business needs, user experience, and long-term maintainability.
  </p>

  <div class="project__gallery pswp-gallery" id="project__gallery">
    {
      images.map((image) => (
        <a
          href={image.src}
          class="image-wrapper"
          data-pswp-width={image.width}
          data-pswp-height={image.height}
          target="_blank"
        >
          <img src={image.src} loading="lazy" alt="ManageSmartr screenshot" />
        </a>
      ))
    }
  </div>

  <CloseModalBtn />
</div>
